WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.511
Heart attack and cardiac arrest are different.

00:00:03.511 --> 00:00:11.218
A heart attack begins with a blocked coronary artery and can progress to cardiac arrest if untreated.

00:00:11.218 --> 00:00:28.619
Warning signs supported by the source include chest or upper-abdominal tightness or discomfort, possible spread towards the left shoulder or arm, neck or lower jaw, sudden breathlessness, sweating, nausea, vomiting or dizziness.

00:00:28.619 --> 00:00:33.808
The source directs calling 995 and going to an Emergency Department.
